---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const entry = {
  "id": "harvard_ii3_31",
  "series": "Band II 3 (1695 - 1700)",
  "seq": 31,
  "text": "<p> [[79.13]] <b>31. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS</p>\n<p> [[79.14]] [Hannover,] 5. (15.) September 1695. [27.46.]</b></p>\n\n[[79.23]] <petit> <e21>Die nicht gefundene Abfertigung unseres Briefes antwortet - wie schon N. 27 - auf N. 25 und wird durch N. 46\n[[79.24]] beantwortet. Am Kopf des Blattes hat Leibniz den Anfang einer vielleicht an Johann Thiele Reinerding, den\n[[79.25]] ersten Sekretär der herzoglichen Bibliothek zu Wolfenbüttel, gerichteten Abfertigung durchgestrichen:\n [[79.26]] \"Insonders großer Herr Ich zweifle nicht derselbe werde das jenige so ihm hinterlaßen, fortgeschicket haben.\n[[80.1]] Zweifle auch nicht, es werde\". Leibniz hat mit Reinerding einen umfänglichen Briefwechsel, besonders zu\n[[80.2]] Katalogisierungsfragen, geführt.</petit> </p>\n<p> [[80.3]] Ex literis meis ad Dn. Vincentium Placcium IC^#'t^#'u^#'m Hamburgensem 5 Septembr. 1695. </p>\n<p> [[80.4]] Quam mirifice sim distractus dici non potest. Varia ex Archivis eruo, antiquas chartas\n[[80.5]] inspicio, M^#'s^#'a inedita conquiro. Ex his lucem dare conor Brunsvicensi Historiae. Magno numero\n[[80.6]] literas et accipio et dimitto. Habeo vero tam multa nova in Mathematicis, tot cogitationes in\n[[80.7]] Philosophicis, tot alias literarias observationes, quas vellem non perire, ut saepe inter agenda\n[[80.8]] anceps haeream, et prope illud Ovidianum sentiam: <i>inopem me copia fecit</i>. Jam 20 et amplius\n[[80.9]] anni sunt, quod Galli Anglique videre meum Instrumentum Arithmeticum sine exemplo novum\n[[80.10]] et a Neperiana Rhabdologia, a Pascaliana Machina pariter et a Morlandiana toto coelo diversum.\n[[80.11]] Nam si numerum ingentem per alium ingentem multiplicare velis, tantum opus est toties\n[[80.12]] rotam quandam promota parte machinae circumagere, quot sunt notae in multiplicatore. Et\n[[80.13]] prodit productum omnibus numeris absolutum, ita ut nulla additione intercalari sit opus. Et\n[[80.14]] parvus an magnus sit numerus multiplicandus non refert, cum res eodem tempore in utroque\n[[80.15]] absolvatur. Ex eo Oldenburgius, et Hugenius, et Arnaldus me per literas suas amicorumve\n[[80.16]] hortati sunt, ut artificii descriptionem in publicum proferrem, sed distuli quod specimen Machinae\n[[80.17]] non nisi exiguum haberem, sufficiens quidem demonstrationi apud artifices, sed non usui\n[[80.18]] apud quoscunque. Tandem vocato ad me opifice nec sumtibus nec tempori peperci donec rem\n[[80.19]] ad perfectionem deduxi, machina confecta, in qua ascendi potest ad numeros duodecim notarum.\n[[80.20]] Annus est quod hoc sum consecutus, retineo tamen adhuc opificem ut alias machinas\n[[80.21]] similes jam paret. Nam passim expetuntur. Describerem libens peculiari dissertatione, sed\n[[80.22]] tempus deest. Inprimis tamen et Dynamicem meam absolvisse vellem; qua veras tandem\n[[80.23]] naturae corporeae leges me complexum puto, ut problemata solvere possim circa corporum\n[[81.1]] actiones inter se, quae per nota hactenus praecepta non habentur. Amici Geometriae interioris a\n[[81.2]] me productae conscii urgent, ut meam infiniti scientiam edam, qua nostrae novae Analyseos\n[[81.3]] fundamenta continentur. Nam Mathesis universalis de quantitate in universum duplex est, agit\n[[81.4]] enim vel de magnitudine finita, et hoc facit Analysis vulgaris seu Algebra (vulgarem voco quae\n[[81.5]] Vietae et Cartesio innotuit), vel de magnitudine infinita, sed quatenus ejus ope finitae magnitudines\n[[81.6]] inveniuntur. Et hoc facit Analysis cujus calculum ego produxi quem Hugenius ipse,\n[[81.7]] quamvis maximus Geometra mire probare coeperat; publice professus esse multa tam profunde\n[[81.8]] abdita, ut vix aliter obtineri posse videantur. Adde his novam quam molior Characteristicam\n[[81.9]] situs, et alia multo adhuc generaliora de arte inveniendi. </p>\n<p> [[81.10]] Hi tamen omnes labores mei (si Historicos excipias), pene furtivi sunt. Nam in aulis scis\n[[81.11]] longe alia quaeri atque expectari. Itaque sunt interdum tractanda quae pertinent ad jura gentium\n[[81.12]] principumque, imperii inprimis nostri. Hoc tamen beneficio Principis sum consecutus, ut pro\n[[81.13]] arbitrio possim privatis litibus abstinere. </p>\n<p> [[81.14]] Curabo ut ad Te perferantur tentamenta ex imperato scripta <greek>perì toỹ bandofóroy</greek>,\n[[81.15]] judicii Tui discendi causa nam ne haec quidem Te latent. Interea et <greek>tà ĕristikà</greek> tractanda\n[[81.16]] persaepe fuere, cum Neostadiensi et Meldensi Episcopis cum Pelissonio aliisque, qui cum\n[[81.17]] moderationem magnam prae se tulerint, nihil vicissim a nostra parte humanitatis reliquum\n[[81.18]] factum est, sed in rebus ipsis cura opus fuit, ne quid res nostrae detrimenti caperent. Et insignes\n[[81.19]] Theologi meas meditationes non sprevere. Quantum vero id mihi cumulum literarum ac\n[[81.20]] dissertatiuncularum peperit, neque editarum licet, neque edendarum, dici vix potest. </p>\n<p> [[81.21]] Haec vero alibi fere dissimulata Tibi, de cujus candore multum mihi polliceor, ideo scribo,\n[[81.22]] ut facilius ignoscas meditationem circa <i>accessiones</i> Tuas differre coacto. Do tamen operam\n[[81.23]] adhibito quodam juvene, ut nonnullae meae meditationes juridicae in ordinem redigantur; quas\n[[81.24]] tuo judicio subjiciam lubens. </p>\n",
  "number": "31.",
  "title": "LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS",
  "date": "[Hannover,] 5. (15.) September 1695. [27.46.]"
};
---

<Layout title={`${entry.title || entry.id} - Leibniz Writings`}>
  <article data-pagefind-body>
    <header class="entry-header">
      <h1 data-pagefind-meta="title">{entry.title || entry.id}</h1>

      <div class="entry-meta">
        {entry.date && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Date:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="date">{entry.date}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Series:</strong>
          <span data-pagefind-meta="series">{entry.series}</span>
        </div>

        {entry.number && (
          <div class="meta-item">
            <strong>Number:</strong>
            <span data-pagefind-meta="number">{entry.number}</span>
          </div>
        )}

        <div class="meta-item">
          <strong>Sequence:</strong>
          <span>{entry.seq}</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- View Toggle -->
    <div class="view-controls">
      <button id="translation-view-btn" class="view-btn active">Translation View</button>
      <button id="scholarly-view-btn" class="view-btn">Scholarly View</button>
    </div>

    <div class="entry-content" data-pagefind-meta="excerpt:31. LEIBNIZ AN VINCENT PLACCIUS [Hannover,] 5. (15.) September 1695. [27.46.] Die nicht gefundene Abfertigung unseres Briefes antwortet - wie schon N. 27 - auf N. 25 und wird durch N. 46 beantwortet. Am Kopf des Blattes hat Leibniz den Anfang einer vielleicht an Johann Thiele Reinerding, den ersten ...">

      <!-- Translation-friendly continuous text -->
      <div id="translation-view" class="text-view active">
        <div class="translation-notice">
          <p><strong>📖 Translation View:</strong> Continuous text optimized for browser translation tools.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="continuous-text" translate="yes" lang="unknown" id="continuous-text">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
        <div class="line-numbers-reference" id="line-numbers-ref">
          <!-- Will be populated by JavaScript -->
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed scholarly view with line numbers -->
      <div id="scholarly-view" class="text-view">
        <div class="scholarly-notice">
          <p><strong>📚 Scholarly View:</strong> Original text with line number annotations preserved.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="annotated-text" id="annotated-text">
          {entry.text.split('\n').map(paragraph =>
            paragraph.trim() && <p set:html={paragraph} />
          )}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>

  <nav class="entry-navigation">
    <a href="/" class="back-link">← Back to Search</a>
  </nav>
</Layout>

<style>
  .entry-header {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border);
  }

  .entry-header h1 {
    color: var(--primary);
    font-size: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .entry-meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
  }

  .meta-item {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 8px;
  }

  .meta-item strong {
    color: var(--text);
    min-width: 80px;
  }

  .meta-item span {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    flex: 1;
  }

  .entry-content {
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .text-content {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 30px;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  .text-content :global(p) {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }

  .text-content :global(p:last-child) {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .text-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .entry-navigation {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-top: 20px;
  }

  .back-link {
    color: var(--primary);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-weight: 500;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .back-link:hover {
    color: var(--primary-dark);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* View Toggle Controls */
  .view-controls {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 20px;
  }

  .view-btn {
    background: transparent;
    border: 2px solid var(--border);
    padding: 8px 16px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    transition: all 0.2s;
  }

  .view-btn:hover {
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .view-btn.active {
    background: var(--primary);
    border-color: var(--primary);
    color: white;
  }

  /* Text Views */
  .text-view {
    display: none;
  }

  .text-view.active {
    display: block;
  }

  /* Translation View */
  .translation-notice, .scholarly-notice {
    background: var(--background);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 12px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .continuous-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 2px solid var(--primary);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 25px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }

  .line-numbers-reference {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 13px;
    padding: 10px;
    background: var(--background);
    border-radius: 4px;
  }

  /* Scholarly View */
  .annotated-text {
    background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 20px;
  }

  .text-line {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    gap: 12px;
  }

  .line-refs {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 4px;
    min-width: 80px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
  }

  .line-num {
    background: var(--primary);
    color: white;
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: monospace;
  }

  .line-content {
    flex: 1;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .line-content :global(b) {
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--primary);
  }

  .line-content :global(i) {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .entry-meta {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .view-controls {
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    .text-line {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 6px;
    }

    .line-refs {
      min-width: auto;
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  // Process text for translation view
  function processTextForTranslation(text) {
    if (!text) return { translationText: '', lineNumbers: [] };

    const lines = text.split('\n');
    let translationText = '';
    const lineNumbers = [];

    lines.forEach(line => {
      const trimmedLine = line.trim();
      if (!trimmedLine) return;

      // Extract line numbers
      const lineNumberMatch = trimmedLine.match(/\[\[(\d+\.\d+)\]\]/g);
      const extractedNumbers = lineNumberMatch ?
        lineNumberMatch.map(m => m.replace(/\[|\]/g, '')) : [];

      // Remove line number markers and HTML tags for continuous text
      let contentOnly = trimmedLine
        .replace(/\[\[\d+\.\d+\]\]/g, '')
        .replace(/<\/?[^>]+(>|$)/g, '')
        .replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
        .trim();

      if (contentOnly) {
        if (translationText) translationText += ' ';
        translationText += contentOnly;
        lineNumbers.push(...extractedNumbers);
      }
    });

    return {
      translationText: translationText.trim(),
      lineNumbers: lineNumbers
    };
  }

  // View switching and text processing
  document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', () => {
    const translationBtn = document.getElementById('translation-view-btn');
    const scholarlyBtn = document.getElementById('scholarly-view-btn');
    const translationView = document.getElementById('translation-view');
    const scholarlyView = document.getElementById('scholarly-view');
    const continuousTextDiv = document.getElementById('continuous-text');
    const lineNumbersRef = document.getElementById('line-numbers-ref');

    // Process the text for translation view
    if (continuousTextDiv && lineNumbersRef && entry && entry.text) {
      const processed = processTextForTranslation(entry.text);
      continuousTextDiv.textContent = processed.translationText;

      if (processed.lineNumbers.length > 0) {
        lineNumbersRef.innerHTML = `<small><strong>Line numbers:</strong> ${processed.lineNumbers.join(', ')}</small>`;
      }
    }

    // View switching functionality
    if (translationBtn && scholarlyBtn && translationView && scholarlyView) {
      translationBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        translationBtn.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyBtn.classList.remove('active');
        translationView.classList.add('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.remove('active');
      });

      scholarlyBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
        scholarlyBtn.classList.add('active');
        translationBtn.classList.remove('active');
        scholarlyView.classList.add('active');
        translationView.classList.remove('active');
      });
    }
  });
</script>